  "source": "user",
  "notes": "Transcribed from TupperDMX's OFL file fixtures/blinder.json, 8ch mode. busk colour needs red, green and blue, so the four white dies are four elements, each dimmed by its own channel: Cold 1, Cold 2, Warm 1, Warm 2 (e.g. 201.3 thru 201.4 is the warm pair). The master brightness channel is a control held at 255, so the grand master and blackout dim the dies once, not twice. The built-in program and its speed are control channels held at 0 (manual). Strobe 8-255 is 0.5-10 Hz, mapped linearly; it is on Cold 1, the element that holds the fixture-wide channels.",
  "physical": { "maxStrobeHz": 10 },
